// hand.
//
// The tables are the published PSTAR (proton) and ASTAR (alpha) tabulations, in
// MeV cm2/g against kinetic energy in MeV - a *mass* stopping power, so a dE/dx in
// MeV/mm is the table value times the density in g/cm3, divided by ten.
//
// Geant4 loads them into a G4PhysicsFreeVector with spline interpolation, so
// reproducing its numbers between the grid points needs the spline as well as the
// table: the grids are 60 and 78 points across a Bragg peak, where linear
// interpolation is low in the curvature and high on the flanks. The second derivatives
// are the not-a-knot ones from G4PhysicsVector::ComputeSecDerivative1.
//
// Accessors rather than plain arrays, following data/icru73qo_tables.cuh: a
// function-local static in a __host__ __device__ function is how this project carries a
// large constant table to both sides of the machine.
